# Windswept Heath: "{T}, Pay 1 life, Sacrifice this land: Search your library for a Forest or Plains card, put it onto the
# battlefield, then shuffle." The search is for a card with a land type (CR 205.3i, 305.6), so it may find a nonbasic land
# with that type - Hallowed Fountain, a Plains Island - and a shockland found this way still asks its controller to pay
# 2 life (CR 614.12a). It may not find an Island, a Swamp, or Blooming Marsh (a land with no basic land type), each refused
# beside the Hallowed Fountain it may find (the positive control). The Heath is sacrificed and the 1 life paid.

[Bot1 Deck]
Windswept Heath
Plains x6
Island
Swamp
Blooming Marsh
Hallowed Fountain
Forest
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Windswept Heath.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Windswept Heath.Activate
! Bot1.Search(Island)
! Bot1.Search(Swamp)
! Bot1.Search(Blooming Marsh)
Bot1.Search(Hallowed Fountain)
Bot1.Accept
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Windswept Heath
Bot1.Battlefield = Hallowed Fountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Hallowed Fountain.Tapped = false
